  "notes": "Two consequences modeled separately because they stem from two distinct downstream failure modes (loss of reverse-flow prevention vs. potential blockage of TDAFW steam path) both traced to the same disc-separation failure. 2-MS-4A path is explicitly stated as available/adequate during the event, justifying BACKED_UP_BY; the Appendix R fire scenario discussion involving 2-MS-4B, disconnect switches, and Unit 3 cross-tie power is design-basis/safety-analysis context describing an unlikely compound scenario, not a stated operable backup during this actual event, so it was not modeled as a System/Component node or edge. EIIS section only lists SB and V; TDAFW pump has no EIIS code given so left null."
